# Changing the target of an ability on the stack judges the new target by the ability's own text (CR 115.7a), fixed as it
# was put on the stack (CR 603.3, 113.7a). Rattlechains enters and its trigger targets Spirit of the Labyrinth ("target
# Spirit gains hexproof"). In response Artificial Evolution replaces Spirit with Horror in Rattlechains' text, then Bot1
# activates Spellskite ("change the target of target spell or ability to Spellskite"). Spellskite is a Horror, but the
# ability still says "target Spirit", so Spellskite is no legal target for it and the target stays: the Spirit of the
# Labyrinth gains hexproof.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Spirit of the Labyrinth
Spellskite
Rattlechains
Artificial Evolution
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spirit of the Labyrinth.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spellskite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Rattlechains.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Spirit of the Labyrinth)
Bot1.Hand.Artificial Evolution.Cast(Rattlechains)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Spirit)
Bot1.Modes(Horror)
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Spellskite.Activate(Stack.Rattlechains)
Bot1.Modes()
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit of the Labyrinth.Keywords = Hexproof
Bot1.Battlefield.Spellskite.Keywords = (absent)
